                <pb facs="0411" n="404" sameAs="frus:frus1937v03/pg404"/>

                <head>Chapter IV: August 13–31, 1937</head>
                <p>Commencement of hostilities at Shanghai between Chinese and Japanese forces,
                    August 13; American protest to China concerning bombing of International
                    Settlement; representations to China and Japan concerning fighting at Shanghai,
                    August 14; U. S. Marine reinforcements from San Diego for Shanghai, August 17;
                    mutual recriminations over situation at Shanghai by China and Japan; failure to
                    reach compromise to stop hostilities there; American representations to Tokyo
                    regarding safety of Tsingtao as undefended city, August 23; announcement of
                    nonaggression pact between China and Soviet Union, August 28–29</p>










































































































































